        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://edgeworthborough.org/home/borough-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A railroad stop established in 1851 near what is now Seminary Lane evolved into the town of Edgeworth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://edgeworthborough.org/home/borough-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Edgeworth sits on the Ohio River, about 14 miles northwest of Pittsburgh, offering scenic river views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
